		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>terference. ChatVLA demonstrates competitive performance on visual question-answering datasets and significantly surpasses state-of-theart vision-language-action (VLA) methods on multimodal understanding benchmarks. Notably, it achieves a six times higher performance on MMMU and scores 47.2% on MM-Star with a more parameter-efficient design than ECoT. Furthermore, ChatVLA demonstrates superior performance on 25 real-world robot manipulation tasks compared to existing VLA methods like OpenVLA. Our findings highlight the potential of our unified framework for achieving both robust multimodal understanding and effective robot control.</p>
			</abstract>
